# Line-ending policy: normalize all text files to LF in the repository and on
# checkout, on every platform. This roots out cross-platform CRLF/LF drift:
# Windows editors and tools may write CRLF into a file, but git normalizes line
# endings when diffing and committing, so diffs stay minimal (no whole-file
# CRLF churn) and the Linux CI checkout matches the stored LF blobs byte-for-byte.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never apply line-ending normalization.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.bmp binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary
